d in 2000 and the recipient of the CBC Canadian Literary Award for short fiction in 2001. Her books have been ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"ad4630ed381eb1bd1c913ea38d6d6258b834e73f319bd119f81a8fc9db8e6bc1\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"6e28ed3dc8221ad292e5342b4e3cd0ff14c14d92888fbcda4a2850c4f3334c8f\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"literary award created 2000s international book prize\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d1\"},\"ref\":\"d1\",\"snippet\":\" ... Metcalf Award, American Academy of Arts and Letters, 2000\\n\\n- Boston University Alumni Award, 2000\\n\\n- Best Debut, The New Yorker Book Awards, 2000\\n\\n- Finalist, Art Seidenbaum Award for First Fiction, Los Angeles Times Book Prize, 2000\\n\\n- \\\"Books to Remember,\\\" citation, New York Public Library, 2000\\n\\n- New York Times Notable ... \",\"title\":\"https://barnard.edu/profiles/jhumpa-lahiri\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d11\"},\"ref\":\"d11\",\"snippet\":\" ... Best Serial Book\\n\\nJim Kacian, Editor. Tug of the Current: Red Moon Anthology of English-Language Haiku 2004. Winchester, VA: Red Moon Press, 2005.\\n\\nAward for Best Book of Haiga:\\n\\nJeanne Emrich, Editor. Reeds: Contemporary Haiga 2005. Edina, MN: Lone Egret Press, 2005.\\n\\nMerit Books Awards\\n\\nfor books ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.hsa-haiku.org/meritbookawards/merit-book_archive.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d12\"},\"ref\":\"d12\",\"snippet\":\" ... She translated the work into English, and during this time she also began translating Italian-language books by other authors. Her translation of Domenico Starnone's Trick (2018) was a finalist for a National Book Award for translated literature. These experiences inspired the essay collection Translating Myself and ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Jhumpa-Lahiri\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d13\"},\"ref\":\"d13\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chronicle, 2000s), encouraged by Murakami himself. Both were later re-translated from Japanese.\\n\\nSince 1999\\n\\nSputnik Sweetheart was first published in 1999, followed by Kafka on the Shore in 2002, with the English translation following in 2005. Kafka on the Shore won the World Fantasy Award in 2006 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haruki_Murakami\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Polish Book of Monsters (edited and translated by Michael Kandel, 2010) is another translation of the short story \\\"The Witcher\\\" which had previously been published in The Witcher, The Last Wish, and Chosen by Fate: Zajdel Award Winner Anthology.\\n*Something Ends, Something Begins (, 2000), 8 stories. Only ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrzej_Sapkowski\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her biography has been translated into 19 different languages.\\n\\nMichaël Dudok de Wit (Dutch pronunciation: [ˈmixaːɛl ˈdydɔɡ də ˈʋɪt]; born 15 July 1953) is a Dutch animator, director and illustrator based in London. He won an Academy Award for Best Animated Short Film for Father and Daughter (2000 ... \",\"title\":\"https://pantheon.world/profile/occupation/film-director/country/netherlands\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d16\"},\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... Three of his stories have been adapted for puppet shows and some poems and stories have also been translated into other languages. His children's works include the picture book Klobuk gospoda Konstantina (Mr Constantine's hat, 2007), winner of the Original Slovenian Picture Book Award in 2008 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ibby.org/subnavigation/archives/hans-christian-andersen-awards/2020\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d17\"},\"ref\":\"d17\",\"snippet\":\" ... In Praise of the Music of Language is a long book devoted to language and translation, especially poetry translation, and one of its leitmotifs is a set of 88 translations of \\\"Ma Mignonne\\\", a highly constrained poem by 16th-century French poet Clément Marot. In this book, Hofstadter ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douglas_Hofstadter\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d18\"},\"ref\":\"d18\",\"snippet\":\" ... For many years he taught … Read More\\n\\nAnne Michaels\\n\\nAnne Michaels is a novelist and poet. Her books have been translated into more than fifty languages and have won dozens of international awards, including the Orange Prize, the Guardian Fiction Prize, the Lannan Award for Fiction, and the ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d19\"},\"ref\":\"d19\",\"snippet\":\" ... Four volumes of his poetry were translated into Hebrew by Muhammad Hamza Ghaneim: Bed of a Stranger (2000), Why Did You Leave the Horse Alone? (2000), State of Siege (2003), and Mural (2006). Salman Masalha, a bilingual Arabic-Hebrew writer, translated his book Memory for Forgetfulness into Hebrew ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahmoud_Darwish\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"2ab2eeb81826da8ade045c74488e1171c212e02b7d7206b981bcb25f434a55dd\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"ee796a9fee2c13bf01f02e852d2f39ae4c32265589a2d3308ab15e2a85cc8b76\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"book award founded 2000s translated many languages\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d4\"},\"ref\":\"d4\",\"snippet\":\" ... Established by Barbara Kingsolver in 2000 and funded entirely by her, it is awarded biennially to the author of a previously unpublished novel of high literary caliber that exemplifies the prize's founding principles.\\n\\nThe PEN/Faulkner Award for Fiction is a national prize which honors the best ... \",\"title\":\"https://americanwritersmuseum.org/literary-links/literary-awards/?srsltid=AfmBOooYIGTV-EUbGd9xDLmBUtcV_Ts9VM7oqhh4K0lfwTLcUoKmITFg\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... the International Booker Prize since the Man Group ended its association with the prizes in 2019.\\n\\nA Russian version of the Booker Prize was created in 1992 called the Booker-Open Russia Literary Prize, also known as the Russian Booker Prize. In 2007, Man Group plc established the ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d8\"},\"ref\":\"d8\",\"snippet\":\" ... The entry fee is $20 and the top prize is $350.\\n\\nThe Fiddlehead's Annual Contests\\n\\nAnnual contests offered by The Fiddlehead literary magazine include fiction and nonfiction contests with a top prize of $2000.\\n\\nThe Malahat Review Writing Contests\\n\\nTop Prizes for these contests range from $1000 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.dreamerswriting.com/writing-contests-in-canada/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d20\"},\"ref\":\"d20\",\"snippet\":\" ... 1935\\n\\nThe is a Japanese literary award presented biannually. Because of its prestige and the considerable attention the winner receives from the media, it is, along with the Naoki Prize, one of Japan's most sought after literary prizes.\\n\\nHistory\\n\\nThe Akutagawa Prize was established in 1935 by ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akutagawa_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d21\"},\"ref\":\"d21\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2024-01-01\\n---\\nReceiving a literary award is a dream of many authors, a sign that they've \\\"made it\\\" right up there with becoming a best seller.\\n\\nIn the literary world, there are thousands of different prizes awarded to aspiring and established authors each year (check out ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.tckpublishing.com/prestigious-literature-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d22\"},\"ref\":\"d22\",\"snippet\":\" ... literary magazines\\n\\nReferences\\n\\nExternal links\\n\\n*Official Site\\n* Reviews NOON 2012\\n* Reviews NOON 2009 Cover to Cover Part 1\\n* Reviews NOON 2009 Cover to Cover Part 2\\n\\nCategory:Literary magazines published in the United States\\nCategory:Annual magazines published in the United States\\nCategory:Magazines established in 2000\\nCategory ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noon_(magazine)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d23\"},\"ref\":\"d23\",\"snippet\":\" ... The first cultural prizes were probably the ancient Greek drama and art competitions, but literary awards as we know them are fairly recent. They came to prominence at the beginning of the twentieth century, with the establishment of the Nobel Prize for Literature in 1901 and the Prix ... \",\"title\":\"https://giramondopublishing.com/heat/archive/beth-driscoll-how-prizes-work-in-the-literary-economy/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d24\"},\"ref\":\"d24\",\"snippet\":\" ... Recent Winner\\n\\nprevious Winner (2024)\\n\\nThe Griffin Poetry Prize\\n\\nAwarded annually to one Canadian and one international poet or translator. It is based on their work from the previous year. The prize is named after Scott Griffin and was established in 2000.\\n\\nRecent Winners\\n\\nprevious Winners (2023)\\n\\nWorking ... \",\"title\":\"https://rocketexpansion.com/book-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d3\"},\"ref\":\"d3\",\"snippet\":\" ... National Book Award – Blonde\\\"National Book Awards – 2000\\\". NBF. Retrieved April 14, 2014.\\n* 2000: Bram Stoker Award (Long Fiction) - In Shock\\n* 2001: Locus Award (Novelette) - In Shock\\n* 2001: International Horror Guild Award, best Short Fiction, for Angel of Mercy\\n* 2002: Los Angeles Book Prize, Best Young Adult Novel ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joyce_Carol_Oates\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d10\"},\"ref\":\"d10\",\"snippet\":\" ... Wisconsin Arts Board Fellowship\\n\\n2000: Orange Prize longlisted - What the Body Remembers\\n\\nCommonwealth Writers Prize (best book from the Canada/Caribbean region) - What the Body Remembers\\n\\n1997: CBC Radio/Canada Council Literary Award (short story category) - \\\"Satya\\\"\\n\\n1996: Friends of American Writers Award - English Lessons and Other Stories ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"2e58aab77dc37384ee64358dee61bab44fe4f2c146e146322a1ffa484f2da7b2\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"fde20129c1f4d2bfd215bae1270d914696c5025422d0323bcfb47266b9808aed\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"international literary prize established 2000s\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_34fb2b49fbba4d8bae1f33e4"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d25\"},\"ref\":\"d25\",\"snippet\":\" ... borders, climate change, language, and forced migration.\\n\\n\\\"Scattered All Over the Earth\\\" is one of two dystopian novels on the longlist for this year's National Book Award for Translated Literature, along with Olga Ravn's \\\"The Employees,\\\" a workplace satire set aboard a twenty-second-century spaceship ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-2022-national-book-awards-longlist-translated-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d26\"},\"ref\":\"d26\",\"snippet\":\" ... s research over the last twenty-five years has focused on the cross-cultural study of environmental storytelling, that is, \\\"the way in which environmental crises that look similar or identical from a scientific point of view are narrated differently in different regions and languages.\\\" The UCLA professor ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.biophilia-fbbva.es/en/noticias/ursula-heise-storytelling-awareness-environmental-crisis-biophilia-award/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d27\"},\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... Eco-Translation: Translation and Ecology in the Age of the Anthropocene.\\n\\nLondon and New York: Routledge, 2016.\\n\\nCronin, Michael. The Expanding World: Towards a Politics of Microspection. Winchester and\\n\\nWashington: Zero Books, 2012.\\n\\nCronin, Michael. Translation and Identity. London and New York: Routledge, 2013.\\n\\nDamrosch, David. What is ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/327409406_Planetary_Figurations_Intensive_Genre_in_World_Literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d28\"},\"ref\":\"d28\",\"snippet\":\" ... had been translated into so many other languages. She seemed to be a prominent poet from Central America and was living in exile in Majorca. I had just published Gathering the Tribes, and I had the naïveté, I was quite a young person—\\n\\ndeNiord: Twenty-six.\\n\\nF