n Prize, the Lannan Award for Fiction, and the Commonwealth Poetry Prize for the Americas. Among many other honours, she is a Royal … Read More ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d39\"},\"ref\":\"d39\",\"snippet\":\" ... Neel Mukherjee is the author of three novels: A Life Apart (2010), which won the Writers' Guild of Great Britain Award for Best Fiction Book; The Lives of Others (2014), which was shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize and the Costa Best Novel Award, and won the Royal ... \",\"title\":\"https://pen.org/meet-the-2021-literary-awards-judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d16\"},\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her novels explore various themes of politics, history, love, adventure and fantasy and have been translated into more than 22 languages. She has been awarded most French prizes in the field of children's books and she was selected for the 2010 IBBY Honour List for the story ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ibby.org/subnavigation/archives/hans-christian-andersen-awards/2020\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"3af4a60ad6da84ad5258176b75d8d7e99d8c6691fdc5ddd7a63e7140341befa1\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"54545288d79686e93cedb8cd446ffb285cb564384e332d50f3a56ad9a64b016d\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"novel translated 25 languages award shortlist 2010s\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_ff1288b8bc1143e385a61f14"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle. The key constraint is \"the award itself was originally created in the 2000s.\" The International Booker Prize was established in 2005 (originally as the Man Booker International Prize). Let me explore this angle, and also consider the Dublin Literary Award (established 2006).\n\nLet me search for books translated into 25+ languages that were contenders for the International Booker Prize.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"International Booker Prize shortlist book translated 25 languages\", \"Man Booker International Prize contender novel translated many languages 2010s\", \"International Dublin Literary Award shortlist translated over twenty languages\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_d0327929e3cb4a19afdc695d","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"novel translated 30 languages shortlisted International Booker Prize\", \"book translated more than 25 languages International Booker Prize contender\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_465f29309b4f43d2881c03f5","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d38\"},\"ref\":\"d38\",\"snippet\":\" ... In a news conference earlier today, International Booker Prize jury chair Frank Wynne credited independent publishers with the lion's share of translated work. \\\"Nobody is surprised that the majority of books on the long- and shortlist,\\\" he said, \\\"are independent publishers. Small independent presses have done enormous ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d41\"},\"ref\":\"d41\",\"snippet\":\" ... The International Booker Prize 2023 Shortlist\\n\\nAt London Book Fair: Insights Into Translation Buyers\\n\\nAs the news of the International Booker Prize shortlist was announced to the public amid the raucous noise and crush of simultaneously programmed events at London Book Fair's opening today (April 17), the ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2023/04/london-book-fair-the-bookers-new-data-on-translation-buyers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2016, the award was significantly reconfigured, and is now given annually to a single book in English translation, with a £50,000 prize for the winning title, shared equally between author and translator. The award has been known as the International Booker Prize since the Man Group ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... Prophet Song by Paul Lynch + Book Club Discussion Guide\\n\\nBooker International Prize\\n\\nA counterpart to the Booker Prize, the International Booker Prize is awarded annually for the finest single work of fiction from around the world that has been translated into English and published in the UK and ... \",\"title\":\"https://bookclubs.com/blog/2023-2024-book-awards-and-book-prize-winners\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... Taylor |\\n| 2003 The Booker Prizes |url= |access-date=2022-10-19 |website=thebookerprizes.com |language=en |archive-date=28 November 2022 |archive-url= |url-status=live }} | Shortlist | Damon Galgut | The Good Doctor | Atlantic Books | *John Carey (Chair) *A. C. Grayling *Francine Stock * Rebecca Stephens MBE *D. J. Taylor ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... of the smallest publisher ever to win the prize, husband-and-wife indie Sort Of Books. In 2022, all the glittering literary prizes went to indies – not only the Booker, but its sister prize for translated fiction, the International Booker, as well as the Nobel, the Goldsmiths, the ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/16/uk-indie-publishing-mavericks-shook-up-books-booker-nobel-fitzcarraldo-sort-of-books-daunt\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen